     "result_text_tail": "th 18. The slide says this.\n- **Two figures are partly assumed:**\n  - Per-store losses assume stores reach the median volume.\n  - The Zipcart test assumes rider speed stays the same and the fee is kept in full.\n\n  Both are labelled as estimates, with their assumptions shown on the slide and live formulas in the workbook.\n- **Path to profitability:** the software case covers the hires' cost, but it is not yet a full path to profitability. At today's burn the company reaches the 12-month runway minimum in month 18 even with no new spending. The pack has no cost breakdown, so the deck makes a burn plan a next step instead of sizing it.\n- **Rounding:** tables and number cards show one decimal (\u2212$6.2), while charts and titles show cents. Slides where this happens carry a rounding footnote.\n- **Pop-up data:** the pack's \"22% still ordering in month three\" comes from a six-week pop-up. I used it as given.\n\n**Numbers:** every one of the 139 numbers traces to the briefing pack or to a calculation from it, with live formulas in the workbook. No placeholders remain, and there were no web sources to re-check.\n\nThe deck has 21 slides: 12 content slides with dividers, one backup slide with the full per-order calculation, and next steps.\n\nNext, I could add a slide modelling the software path to profitability if you can share a cost breakdown, or switch the theme.\n\nFiles are in `./deliverable/`:\n- `parcelbird-now.pptx`\n- `parcelbird-now-sources.xlsx`\n- `parcelbird-now.json`\n- `build-spec.py`"
